quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  20,52,He (Moses) said: ‘Their knowledge is with My Lord in a Book. My Lord neither makes any error nor forgets.’
  20,53,"(He is) the One Who made the earth a habitable cradle for you and made therein ways and means (of livelihood) for you and sent down water from the sky. Then, through it, We have brought out various pairs of vegetation."
  20,54,Eat and graze your cattle. There are indeed signs in this for those who possess intelligence.
  20,55,"From it (i.e. the soil of the earth) did We create you, and into it shall We return you, and from it shall We bring you out another time."
  20,56,"And indeed, We showed him (i.e. Pharaoh) all Our signs, but he rejected (them) and refused (to believe)."
  20,57,"He said: ‘Have you come to us to expel us from our land with your magic, O Musa (Moses)?"
  20,58,"So we shall confront you with magic like it. Therefore, set a time (for the contest) between us and you, which neither we shall break nor you, at a central location.’"
  20,59,"He (Moses) said: ‘Your appointment will be on the Day of Adornment (i.e. the day of Annual Festival), and let the people be gathered at mid-morning.’"
  20,60,Then Pharaoh turned away (to consult his cabinet). He put together his strategy and arrived (at the arena).
  20,61,"Musa (Moses) said to them (i.e. the sorcerers): ‘Woe to you! Do not fabricate a lie against Allah, lest He should destroy you with a punishment. Whoever fabricates (lies) will lose surely.’"
  20,62,So they debated their plan among themselves and kept their confidential discourse secret.
  20,63,They (the sorcerers) said: ‘These two are only magicians who want to expel you from your land with their magic and abolish your exemplary tradition.
  20,64,"So, gather your strategy and line up in rows (for the contest). Indeed, he will prosper today who gains the upper hand.’"
